A||N||15||Ozzy||More Problems...||||5
Z||000000||Ozzy||09-26-1999||11:36 PM||||Hi Humans...<P>Well, my '88 coupe is over it's belt tensioner problem but a new one has reared it's ugly head.<P>Sometimes when I go to start it now...Nada! It turns over fine but feels like no spark type problem. But if I persist for a time eventually it lights up. The first time it did it, it kinda coughed and farted a couple of times like it wanted to try to start. As I said with persistence it finally started. When it is running it feels like normal. No other symptoms that I can detect. I'm noticing some small temp fluctuations that I have not seen before but they don't seem that great. <P>Is the DIS system on the 2.5L a unit that will give intermittent problems? Or is it like the CDI type systems that either work or they don't? It has only started happening in the last 2 days and I have done nothing else to the car recently.<P>Thnx<P>Ozzy||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||09-27-1999||02:26 AM||||Could be that one of the temp sensors is giving erratic readings. If the temp sensor to the ECM is feeding it with temperatures that are too high, the mixture will not be right for cold starts...||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||09-27-1999||09:43 AM||||check all those ground leads,,, there's like a dozen ends to check. one of them loose could be trouble.<P>ususally DIS works or it doesn't. The crank sensor is ok or it wouldn't run at all. check all the plugs and wires. If a wire even looks bad replace the set. DIS does not like it if a wire or plug is marginal.<P>check the thin leads off the battery too.... you might have whacked one while you were fooling with the tensioner. these can cause weak spark. The whole car runs off the thin red lead. the fat end only goes to the starter.<P>Oh,,, wait..... I can't answer this..... I'm not a human. 8) <p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 09-27-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ozzy||09-28-1999||11:28 PM||||It starts when cool an runs a little while the just shuts down dead...won't start again 'till it cools but it is not an over heating problem and both coolant sensors are new...<P>Going to pick the little bastard up on a trailer tomorrow!!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ozzy||10-02-1999||03:47 AM||||So ogre... If a coil or plug or plug wire is poor or bad, the engine will shut down dead?? I would think it would at least splutter a little or run weak. <P>I mean when this thing stops it just quits stone dead and won't start again untill it's cooled off. I know it's not over heating so there is no issue with an over hot engine.<P>Ground leads???  I'm not sure even where to start with that one. Seems to me these damn thing shoulda ran a star point grounding system with all the trouble grounding seems to cause. <P>I'm quite despondant with this car at the moment. I luv upgrading and even repairing worn stuff but when it holds me up on the interstate... I just don't have the time for that. <P>Bummed Ozzy||||reg||1
Z||000005||batboy||10-02-1999||11:08 AM||||I saw one case where a 3.1 DIS engine had a hairline crack in one of the three coil packs. It ran pretty good until it warmed up and expanded the crack allowing the spark to jump out the crack. Those coils each run two cylinders, so the 6 cylinder slowly became a 4 cylinder as it warmed up.||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||10-02-1999||09:24 PM||||It dies when hot...... Hmmmmm thats baad.<P>You could have a coil shorting when hot. As I reread this tho..... It could also be the crank sensor.<P>You need to verify for sure if it's getting spark or not. check spark from both coils.<P>No spark from either coil points to a dead controller or crank sensor. These are under the coils.<P><BR>As for grounds.... check every wire you can find that anchors to the block or tranny bell housing. My 87 has 4 on one bell housing bolt. another one on another bell bolt. 2 to the block near the thermotat. and a couple other large straps including the battery lead.<P>I can't think of any other sensor that would die on a DIS motor that it can't run without except the TPS. All others make it run like hell and set errors.<P>I've also heard of people having trouble with the terminal block near the battery. That can kill it. Since you where playing in that area working on the tensioner,,,, you may have whacked the block or some of the wires..... pull it appart, it has a bolt thru it, and check every thing... make sure its all clean and tight.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Ozzy||10-03-1999||03:50 AM||||Ogre...When you say "Bad" on the crank sensor or controller, is that a replacement DIS or are you refering to a tear down to get at the component on the crank itself. The first is not bad to me; the latter however would suck immensley!!<P>I have not had the time to run the car out the highway to make it die and check for spark. Also 88 Fiero e-mailed me to say he had the same problem and replaced "the unit that sends the firing signal from the crank."<BR>I assume he means the crank sensor.<P>Ozzy||||reg||1
Z||000008||theogre||10-03-1999||06:29 PM||||yes, he ment the crank sensor. far as I know it's all under the coils. Check the spark. A fuel pump or f.p. relay could also cause this.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Ozzy||10-04-1999||01:25 AM||||O.K., thnx ogre. I hope to have some time soon to check it out and find the problem(s).<P>You have given me somewhere to start.<P>Ozzy||||reg||1
Z||000010||Ozzy||10-05-1999||10:54 PM||||Hey ogre? Don't mean to drag you from your lair again but...<P>If I bought the scanner you have refered to before and hooked it up to my coupe, blasted of up the highway untill the engine stops again would the scanner give me an accurate idea of what is causing my problem??? <P><BR>Ozzy||||reg||1
Z||000011||theogre||10-06-1999||09:27 AM||||it might. depends on just what it is.<P>the scanner can grab things in real time. but tripping it to trap settings in this particular problem may not tell you much.<P>did you check all the terminal block by the battery yet? Did you check spark?<P>On the other hand, if the ECM is crashing the scanner will tell you for sure. It should also tell you if there is a sensor having a crap. It might tell you if the brick is acting up. depends on just how it's acting up.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||ayamnik||10-06-1999||12:28 PM||||I’m almost 100% sure it’s the pickup coil. I have seen many cars do what you described. My dodge Daytona my Cadillac and so on it’s the pickup coil it’s in the distributor (usually a little circuit or a chip with wires going in it). I don’t know how it it’s on a v6 fiero but on all cars I have worked you take the distributor cap off and rotor than there should be a metal cover round you take it off and their should be a circuit. So try this first My dodge did the same thing startup run warm-up and kill wait for it to cool and you’re good to go. So try it and tell me if I’m right I love being right. ||||reg||4
Z||000013||theogre||10-06-1999||02:17 PM||||aya,<P>from 87 on. this motor is crank timed. no distributor. 2 coils. It's not a 10 minute job. that's why I said check spark.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Ozzy||11-02-1999||12:18 AM||||HEy Folks...I've been kinda busy and posted this thread awhile ago.<P>I've just recently had the time to get back to this problem and finally tore out the ignition mod. after determining No spark after shutdown.<P>Ogre...one more time, you nailed it right on the head. The crank sensor had a bloody big crack almost the whole length of the unit. I bought a replacement and had the Napa store dude test the Ignition mod about 8 times. Put it all back in and she is up and running again.<P>Man I gotta stop predicting the worst everytime something happens on this car.<P>Happy Ozzy!!||||reg||10
